      "message_id": "msg-asst-23b92b83396e",
      "session_id": "sess-mutowu8s-s9ibd",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "- **Definition**: RSI (Relative Strength Index) is a technical indicator used to measure the magnitude and direction of price changes to identify potential overbought or oversold conditions.  \n- **Calculation**: It is calculated by comparing the magnitude of recent gains and losses, with a default period of 14 days. The result ranges from 0 to 100.  \n- **Application**: RSI helps traders determine if a stock is overbought (above 70) or oversold (below 30), guiding decisions on when to buy or sell.  \n- **Limitation**: RSI is most effective in trending markets and can generate false signals in ranging markets.",
